---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { readFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import { resolve } from "node:path";

const dataReleasePointer = JSON.parse(
  await readFile(resolve(process.cwd(), "public/data/quran/manifest.json"), "utf8"),
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Methods & Data | Quran | HadithCritic Projects"
  description="Sources, transformations, coverage, and known limits for the Quran variant browser and research data."
>
  <div class="qm-page hc-container">
    <nav class="qm-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/projects/quran/">Quran</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Methods &amp; Data</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="qm-header">
      <p class="hc-eyebrow">Source policy · release 1</p>
      <h1 class="hc-title hc-title--lg">Methods &amp; Data</h1>
      <p class="qm-lede">
        This page identifies the data behind the variant browser, what the import changes, and which questions remain open. Counts describe this pinned export; they do not establish completeness of the historical record.
      </p>
      <p class="qm-release">Current data release: <code>{dataReleasePointer.releaseId}</code></p>
    </header>

    <section class="qm-section" aria-labelledby="qm-coverage-title">
      <h2 id="qm-coverage-title">Source coverage</h2>
      <div class="qm-table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source layer</th><th scope="col">Imported coverage</th><th scope="col">Use and limit</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/telota/corpus-coranicum-tei/tree/57cb2b7be321ecfba100cb5f7988974f47864a14">Corpus Coranicum TEI</a></th>
              <td>18,000 variant records; 6,236 Cairo Arabic lines; 6,236 transcription lines; 18,822 translation lines; 2,322 manuscript descriptions in the manuscript collection; 15,977 explicit commentary Quran references.</td>
              <td>The site searches all 18,000 variant records and provides candidate-linked passages for 3,492 Cairo verse IDs. The searchable manuscript catalogue covers all 2,322 <code>msDesc</code> records in that collection. The pinned TEI release contains 37,358 source-located text blocks from 85 files, but those text blocks are not currently exposed in a reader. The intertext catalogue indexes 713 <code>msDesc</code> source records and 9,452 selected field elements from 713 files. The relationship index preserves explicit reader links, candidate locators, and exact Quran reference targets. Only publisher-coded <code>#TUK</code> references receive exact intertext links, and only when their target IDs resolve uniquely in the pinned source. No variant record has a linked source-authority key. A strict target pattern yields 13,719 unreviewed TEI-to-Cairo navigation candidates; 2,258 other range forms remain unlinked. The target grammar is undocumented, so none is presented as a verified semantic mapping. Manuscript images have separate rights checks.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Other supplied collections</th>
              <td>Not included in the public site data.</td>
              <td>The supplied Nasser JSON, Studies-folder documents, and Shamela CSV are excluded from this Quran release: they are not ingested, queried, or published. The existing Academic Studies site module remains available.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="qm-section" aria-labelledby="qm-preservation-title">
      <h2 id="qm-preservation-title">What the import preserves</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Source-native TEI identifiers, authority keys, locators, word order, and decoded character data.</li>
        <li>Arabic text, transcription, and each translation as separate layers tied to their source record.</li>
        <li>Manuscript catalogue statements indexed at named TEI paths; each value links to the exact element line and retains source attributes and file hash.</li>
        <li>Original text strings and whitespace; normalization and matching values never replace displayed source text.</li>
        <li>Source record file, pinned commit, file hash, and direct repository line links for every catalog record and candidate locator.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The current word crosswalk follows the source <code>w/@n</code> locator to a Cairo TEI <code>xml:id</code>. It is a mechanical candidate relation. The interface marks each candidate as unreviewed and does not claim that the texts are equivalent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="qm-section" aria-labelledby="qm-limits-title">
      <h2 id="qm-limits-title">Known limits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The browser contains all 18,000 variant records present in this pinned TEI export. It is not a complete reader or searchable edition of every historical reading tradition.</li>
        <li>All 18,000 variant records have empty source-authority keys. Their TEI records are cited; an underlying book, page, or manuscript source is not supplied in this export.</li>
        <li>All 2,322 manuscript descriptions lack native <code>msDesc/@xml:id</code>. The catalogue retains null and uses a within-file element position and source line for navigation.</li>
        <li>Many word entries across the full export have no native locator. Missing locators remain missing.</li>
        <li>Manuscript catalogue descriptions are not direct checks of manuscript images. No manuscript image is included; third-party image rights require separate review.</li>
        <li>The pinned TEI text blocks are not presented as a complete searchable edition. Other TEI structures remain in linked source files.</li>
        <li>The intertext catalogue preserves selected metadata from each <code>msDesc</code>. Its separate <code>categories.xml</code> taxonomy is indexed as 122 source categories, but the TEI records contain no explicit <code>catRef</code> links assigning records to categories.</li>
        <li>The source repository README describes a wider manuscript inventory than the 2,322 descriptions in this pinned manuscript collection. This site reports the imported count and does not claim the wider figure.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="qm-section qm-reuse" aria-labelledby="qm-reuse-title">
      <h2 id="qm-reuse-title">Source and reuse</h2>
      <p>
        The Corpus Coranicum data is pinned to commit <code>57cb2b7be321ecfba100cb5f7988974f47864a14</code>. The repository identifies its TEI data as CC BY-SA 4.0. Attribution: Corpus Coranicum Project, ed. Michael Marx, TEI Data, Berlin-Brandenburg Academy of Sciences and Humanities. The catalog, passage index, and locator fields are modifications; share-alike terms apply to this adapted data.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0 license</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/telota/corpus-coranicum-tei/tree/57cb2b7be321ecfba100cb5f7988974f47864a14">Pinned source repository</a>
      </p>
      <nav class="qm-tools" aria-label="Quran project pages">
        <a class="hc-btn" href="/projects/quran/read/">Read &amp; compare <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="hc-btn" href="/projects/quran/variants/">Open variant index <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="hc-btn" href="/projects/quran/relationships/">Relationship index <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="hc-btn" href="/projects/quran/intertexts/">Intertext source catalogue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="hc-btn hc-btn--ghost" href="/projects/quran/manuscripts/">Manuscript catalogue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="hc-btn hc-btn--ghost" href="/projects/quran/analyses/">Analyses <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a class="hc-btn hc-btn--ghost" href="/projects/quran/">Return to Quran project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </nav>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .qm-page { padding-block: 2rem clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem); }
  .qm-crumbs { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.65rem; margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5rem); color: var(--hc-text-tertiary); font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .qm-crumbs a, .qm-section a:not(.hc-btn) { color: var(--hc-gold); text-decoration: none; }
  .qm-header { max-width: 64rem; padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hc-rule); }
  .qm-header h1 { margin-block: 0.5rem 1rem; }
  .qm-lede { max-width: 72ch; color: var(--hc-text-secondary); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .qm-release { color: var(--hc-text-tertiary); font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .qm-release code { color: var(--hc-text-primary); font-size: inherit; }
  .qm-section { max-width: 76rem; padding-block: 2.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hc-rule); }
  .qm-section h2 { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--hc-text-primary); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .qm-section p, .qm-section li { max-width: 78ch; color: var(--hc-text-secondary); line-height: 1.75; }
  .qm-section li + li { margin-top: 0.55rem; }
  .qm-section code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; color: var(--hc-text-primary); font-size: 0.86em; }
  .qm-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; }
  th, td { min-width: 11rem; padding: 0.9rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hc-rule); color: var(--hc-text-secondary); vertical-align: top; line-height: 1.65; }
  thead th { color: var(--hc-text-primary); font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  tbody th { color: var(--hc-text-primary); font-weight: 500; }
  .qm-tools { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { th, td { min-width: 9rem; } }
</style>
